WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.749
Scope control protects you and the buyer.

00:00:02.749 --> 00:00:04.320
Ambiguity creates angry refunds.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.462
This lesson is about what's included (and not).

00:00:07.462 --> 00:00:08.248
Scope control.

00:00:08.248 --> 00:00:10.997
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.997 --> 00:00:14.925
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:20.816
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.816 --> 00:00:25.136
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:25.136 --> 00:00:29.064
Stay practical: list includes/excludes before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:32.521
List what is included and what is not.

00:00:32.521 --> 00:00:33.305
Be blunt.

00:00:33.305 --> 00:00:34.089
Be kind.

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:36.050
Remember the objective: list includes/excludes.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.363
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:45.068
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.068 --> 00:00:49.382
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:54.087
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.832
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.832 --> 00:00:58.400
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.995
Call out edge cases: revisions, response time, and what happens if they stall.

00:01:03.995 --> 00:01:06.024
Remember the objective: list includes/excludes.

